A||||13||Fformula88||A Great Evil takes over Motor Trend!!||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||11-30-2001||05:56 PM||||I just got done reading the editorial section in my Jan 02 Motor Trend to discover C Van Tune is stepping down as editor in chief.  The parent company has named David E Davis Jr as the interim Editor in Chief until they decide on a permanent replacement.<P>Many of you will recognize his name as the editor of Automobile Magazine, who in his Oct 2000 issue editorial, blasted nearly everything about the Fiero, and those who own, maintain and try to improve them today while helping to spread rumors and make faceless accusations about the car and its capabilities!  Don't believe me, he claims a large number of GM sedans and station wagons had better handling and road holding capabilities.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Whatever.<P>Needless to say I have already fired off a letter to Motor Trend expressing my concern for the future of the magazine (and my subscription) with that man at the helm!  Anyone else read this?  I still cannot believe it!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||11-30-2001||06:26 PM||||He was probably just angry when he wrote that.  I bet he had just paid twice the price for a car with half the capability.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||11-30-2001||06:50 PM||||Yes, I read that.  Didn't make that connection.  That's a shame.<P>I hope it doesn't change, and they get someone in that spot that is better.<P>Did see they had a story about "Pre owned" Cherokee<P>Wow, finally, I've got something that's "in"<P><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-30-2001||06:54 PM||||Another auto mag slides into the grease pit.<BR>But a new magazine makes its debut in about 2 weeks.  If you're a member of <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>CFOG-I</A>, you'll be receiving a copy.  We encourage you to share it with others!<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000004||kevin||11-30-2001||07:00 PM||||I will bet a dollar to a doughnut that Mr. Davis will pay little attention to letters we send him. I know he should, but realistically, I think he has other issues to contend with. I know he said the things he said, and as we know, the content of his bilge is not worth more than an open sewer in Afghanistan!I will not read Motor Trend except perhaps for an article or two.The morning newspaper does a better job for the parakeet cage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||11-30-2001||07:01 PM||||I have a subscription to Motor Trend, but I'm just not big on it anymore...it seems like every issue is "Battle of the 4 door sedans" or "Battle of the SUV", or some other vehicle that just doesn't do much for me. Car and Driver is going to be my next attempt at a good car magazine. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
