Z||000007||johnt671||11-30-2001||08:24 PM||||Fierolisa, Car & Driver is just as bad.  I subscribed for years and then dropped it because they have more on trucks then cars.  They reply to letters complaining about this by saying as long as truck sales are up they will test them.  I guess I'm one of about 300 people that hate those things and the high fuel usage that I could better use in my Fiero.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Neal||11-30-2001||08:32 PM||||Any 'new car' mag that has the need to bash a 15 year old car is beyond me.  They work with new cars so why does a no longer produced 13-18 year old car even get mentioned in the covers.<P>I know its not a 'new car' mag but Grassroots Motorsports is the absolute best car mag out there.  It truly is a classy quality production.  Ive never read any negative oppinions about any car.  Plus they deal with cars and car guys that are after similar goals as a large number of fiero owners.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fformula88||11-30-2001||10:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>If you're going to send him a letter, make sure you write the address on the envelope with a pen, not a crayon.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I hope thats a joke.<P>Unfortunately all car magazines are featuring mroe 4-door sedans and SUV's since thats about all that is left.  I guess they cannot do a 'Vette vs something else all the time.<P>Actually, the magazine I like to look at now and then (putting on flame suit!) is Sport Compact Car.  Especially for their new car reviews, they seem to do very good writeups and are always driving something sporty!  I know there is also a good share of rice in there, but they are generally testing the modded cars that actually have modifications. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||qwikgta||11-30-2001||11:58 PM||||I'm not sure if everyone can get this mag, but it is pretty good, some rice but a lot of American cars too.  Last month a great article on the J-car (sunfire) and it had some good info on the 2.4 motor too.  I like it cause i can get some ideas every once and a while.  <P>Rob<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HCI.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic_copy.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tigger||12-01-2001||12:50 AM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>I hope thats a joke.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, that's was a joke.  In Automobile Magazine a few months after the article, Davis wrote a response about all the "hate" mail he got.  He mentioned something along the lines of not opening mail written in crayon as an insult.<P>What I find so funny about that article was his clueless fascination that there's still such a following of Fiero owners and enthusiasts.<P>So then he's suprised to get so much mail after writing it.  "Hello Mcfly, anybody home?"     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">    DUH!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
